-- =====================================================================================
-- The full Mathematics question bank: the remaining 11 chapters and 1,456 questions.
--
-- WHY THIS IS A MIGRATION AND NOT A SCRIPT
-- A deployed instance builds its database from migrations alone. Content created by POSTing
-- to a running server exists only on the machine that received the POSTs, so seeding this way
-- is the only way the deployed site has a question bank at all.
--
-- WHY THE PAYLOAD IS DOLLAR-QUOTED JSON
-- The content is LaTeX. It is dense with backslashes and, critically, with '$$' display-maths
-- delimiters. Escaping that into ordinary SQL string literals is a reliable way to corrupt
-- 'rac' into a formfeed or to terminate a string early. Dollar-quoting removes escaping from
-- the problem entirely: the bytes between the tags are taken verbatim. The tags below were
-- checked against the payload for collisions before this file was generated.
--
-- Chapters are keyed by NAME, never by id, so this survives a database rebuilt from scratch
-- where the generated ids differ.
--
-- Content is inserted verbatim, including the blank lines inside a question stem. Those carry
-- paragraph structure and the renderer preserves them; trimming would change how a paper reads.
--
-- markingSchemeId is deliberately absent on every question. A null override means the engine
-- resolves the ACTIVE scheme for the (exam_pattern, question_type) pair when an attempt starts
-- and snapshots it, so JEE Main single-correct gets +4/-1 and JEE Advanced multiple-correct gets
-- partial marking, while a teacher can still correct a scheme later for future attempts.
-- =====================================================================================

